{message: Yeh bahut achha sawaal hai, aur is ka jawab samajhna zaroori hai. "Christ killer" ka matlab hai "Masih ko qatl karne wala", aur ise aksar Yahudi logon ke liye istemal kiya gaya. Lekin yeh ek nafrat bhara lafz (slur) hai, jo Yahudiyon ke khilaf nafrat aur tashaddud ko badhawa deta raha. Is ka sabab yeh tha ke kuch Christian mazhabi tehreeron mein Yahudiyon ko poori qaum ki taur par Yeshu (Jesus) ki maut ka zimmedar thehraya gaya. Is ke baad sadiyon tak Yahudiyon par zulm hota raha: unhein alag basthiyon mein rakha gaya, unpar pabandiyan lagayi gayin, aur kai jagah qatl-e-aam (pogroms) hue.

Tareekhi tor par dekhein to kuch baatein zaroor yaad rakhni chahiye. Mazhabi bayanat mein Yahudiyon ki zimmedari ka zikr hai, lekin Roman hukoomat ne Yeshu ko Roman tareeqe se salib par chadhaya tha, aur Roman governor Pontius Pilate ne faisla kiya tha. Iske ilawa, "poori qaum zimmedar hai" ka khayal tareekhi aur akhlaqi tor par ghalat hai. 1965 mein Catholic Church ne Nostra Aetate jaise bayan ke zariye is collective guilt ko radd kiya.

Yeh sikhta hai ke tareekh ko parhte waqt hum sirf lafzon ko nahi, un ke asar ko bhi samajhte hain. Agar aap kisi kitab mein yeh lafz dekhein, to dekhna ke us waqt ka sabab kya tha aur us se logon ko kya nuqsan hua. Kya aap chahte hain ke main Nostra Aetate ya Medieval Europe mein Yahudiyon ke haalat ke baare mein aur batayun?}

